//! `view.av` — what users meet: a `View` is a component any realizer can
//! draw. A tree is a `List<dyn View>`; only the realizer knows a target,
//! so one component answers every surface. UI.md §19.1–19.2.
use realize.realizer.{Realizer}

/// A component a realizer can draw. The component IS the node: its
/// fields are its props, and this method hands it to the target.
export trait View {
    fn realize(r: dyn Realizer)
}
